        'Put a comma before the final «e» when an earlier «e» already joins two items inside the list, otherwise two coordinating «e» collide: «nei settori dei trasporti, del medicale e delle life sciences, e dell’industria». This is not the Anglo serial comma, which stays forbidden in lists with no internal «e».',
        'For a long <select> of countries, regions or languages, apply ONE policy to every option: either leave the whole list in English, or translate every label AND re-sort it alphabetically on the Italian label, keeping the English value= attributes intact. A list that is 97% English with six Italian labels stranded in their English sort position is a findability bug on a lead form and a stronger tell than an all-English list.',
        'Translate every attribute string, not just visible text: aria-label, title, alt and placeholder. A navigational «home» in a logo aria-label is «pagina iniziale». Leaving one attribute in English while the rest are translated is the partial-pass signature reviewers read as machine translation.',
        'Translate a partial-sentence fragment so it still joins its neighbours after your rewrite. When a heading is stored as separate strings («See how we bring it all» / «together»), rewrite all of them together so they reassemble («Scopra come integriamo ogni» + «elemento»).',
        'When the source wraps a brand name in its own tag, keep the tag around the brand name ONLY; do not extend the span over the translated descriptive words that follow («<span>Lismar</span> controlli non distruttivi», never «<span>Lismar controlli non distruttivi</span>»), which merges two elements and changes the rendering.',
